C={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-thirtieth-d3-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]};P={x["paper_id"]:x for x in json.loads((D/"interspeech-2025-papers.json").read_text())["papers"]}
N={
"emezue25_interspeech":("Speech technology cannot serve a language well when it has too little representative speech and text to learn from.","Web text may be scarce, translated from outside cultures, or concentrated in a few speakers, so simply scraping more text does not guarantee useful speech coverage.","Collect a small convenient corpus or translate English sentences and treat the resulting recordings as representative.","Build the corpus with language communities: generate culturally grounded sentences, review them twice, and record many speakers with controlled diversity.","NaijaVoices uses 100 themes, 144 sentence generators, reviewers, and a facilitator-guided recording application for Igbo, Hausa, and Yoruba; the resulting corpus contains over 1,800 hours, 645K sentences, and 5,455 speakers.","The dataset is an intervention on the training distribution: speaker, topic, language, and sentence diversity are treated as variables that determine what a recognizer can learn; WER tests downstream usefulness.","The paper reports large ASR gains after five-epoch fine-tuning, including an average 42.33% WER improvement for XLSR and stronger multilingual coverage than prior listed resources.","Language coverage, collection process, licensing, transcription quality, and the selected ASR models bound the claim; WER improvement does not establish equal cultural representation or performance for all African languages."),
"gao25d_interspeech":("A speech generator should obey requests about pronunciation, emotion, age, gender, or quality, but judging every generated waveform during training is expensive and listener preferences are hard to turn into a differentiable signal.","Codec language models generate discrete tokens that later become audio through a flow model and vocoder, so an audio-level reward creates a costly feedback loop and may not distinguish competing outputs.","Use ordinary reinforcement learning with rewards computed after full waveform synthesis, or optimize only next-token likelihood.","Predict several task rewards directly from codec tokens and make the reward path differentiable with Gumbel-Softmax, allowing direct back-propagation into the token language model.","DiffRO predicts rewards for ASR, emotion, speech quality, age, and gender from generated codec tokens; a multi-task reward model supplies the signal and the language model is optimized without the full reinforcement-learning loop.","The method replaces a sampled discrete choice with a soft probability over codebook entries during training, so reward gradients can reach token probabilities; the reward is a proxy whose meaning depends on each downstream predictor.","The paper reports improved pronunciation accuracy and state-of-the-art WER results, with controllability experiments for emotion, MOS, age, and gender; codec-level MOS and re-encoded audio reveal disagreement between proxy and waveform quality.","Reward-model accuracy, codec reconstruction, vocoder behavior, sampling, and listener perception bound the result; a differentiable proxy is not the same as human preference or end-to-end quality."),
"jacquelin25_interspeech":("A speaker may increase vocal effort to be heard in noise, but a voice-conversion system should change that effort without changing the words or the person speaking.","Effort changes pitch, spectral slope, vowel resonances, articulation, and timing together, so changing one acoustic knob can damage intelligibility or identity.","Manipulate pitch or energy directly, or put all acoustic variation into one undifferentiated code stream.","Use separate quantized code layers: preserve linguistic content in one layer and encode vocal effort in another so effort can be controlled independently.","LombardTokenizer builds on residual vector quantization, uses mHuBERT for multilingual content, trains a vocal-effort encoder, fine-tunes on loud speech, and tests zero-shot conversion on loud and Lombard datasets.","Quantization assigns different information to discrete codebooks; the experiment asks whether the code carrying effort can be changed while content codes remain stable, measured with WER, speaker error, spectral divergences, and listeners' effort judgments.","The paper reports lower WER and EER than comparison FreeVC systems, including 10.97% WER and 6.67% EER for one AVID configuration, and stronger generalization on unseen Lombard conditions.","The datasets, effort labels, encoder choices, perceptual test, and zero-shot conditions bound the claim; disentanglement is inferred from task behavior, not proven as a unique physical separation."),
"fu25_interspeech":("When several people speak at once, a listener needs to know where each sound comes from in three dimensions, even when there is noise, echo, or no known speaker count.","Two microphones provide interacting time, level, and spectral cues, and overlap makes one spatial pattern contain several sources; a flat classifier must resolve detection and precise angles at once.","Assume one source, restrict the room to a 2-D plane, or regress one angle directly from the whole mixture.","First detect and coarsely partition likely directions, then refine elevation and azimuth with gated features and shared binaural attention.","AuralNet converts left/right audio into gammatone features and cross-correlations, uses coarse sector classification, fine localization, azimuth/elevation regressors, and a weighted multi-task loss; it is tested across source counts, noise, reverberation, and seen/unseen rooms.","The coarse class narrows the search space while regression supplies precision; F1 handles class imbalance in source detection and detection-aware angular error measures directional accuracy.","The paper reports higher detection and F1 scores than DeepEar, including 92.71% F1 for one-talker unseen rooms versus 78.88%, and average azimuth error of 2.92 degrees versus 8.44 degrees.","Room simulation/recording conditions, source geometry, silent-sector imbalance, and the comparison baseline bound the result; strong localization does not establish separation or human listening improvement."),
"gao25g_interspeech":("Meeting transcription fails when speech overlaps, microphones are distant, and a camera sees a speaker whose voice is masked; synchronized visual evidence can help decide who spoke and what was said.","Audio-only systems confuse overlapping speakers and room effects, while visual cues are asynchronous, incomplete, and tied to face visibility and camera placement.","Run an audio recognizer and diarizer independently, or add video without changing the task and data split.","Define matched audio-visual tasks and evaluate systems that align and fuse speech, faces, and multi-device recordings under realistic meeting overlap.","The MISP 2025 challenge supplies 125 hours of synchronized meeting audio/video from 263 participants and 23 rooms, with AV speaker diarization, AV speech recognition, and joint diarization-recognition tracks plus baselines and participant methods.","The challenge makes speaker identity and word identity coupled sequence decisions; DER, CER, and character-phoneme CER measure different failure surfaces rather than one generic score.","The paper reports a top AVSD diarization error rate of 8.33% and a best reported AVSR CER of 9.48%, while noting that audio enhancement and separation remained important in difficult settings.","Challenge splits, language/domain, camera visibility, participant submissions, and track-specific metrics bound the comparison; leaderboard results do not isolate the causal value of vision or guarantee unconstrained meeting performance."),
"chen25p_interspeech":("A speech codec must turn a waveform into a short discrete sequence and reconstruct speech that still sounds and works like the original; using several codebooks adds rate and system complexity.","A single codebook must carry both coarse linguistic structure and fine acoustic detail, while encoder and decoder capacity can become unbalanced during training.","Use residual codebooks with more tokens, or train a mirror-shaped encoder and decoder throughout even when the decoder needs greater capacity.","Train in two stages: first use a mirror architecture to stabilize the codebook, then switch to a stronger non-mirror decoder while preserving the learned quantizer.","DS-Codec uses vector and product quantization with one 8,192-entry codebook, a downsampling encoder, recurrent/transformer decoder components, and time/frequency discriminators; ablations compare mirror and non-mirror stages.","Quantization maps a continuous latent vector to a nearby code; the staged architecture changes which parameters are allowed to adapt after the codebook has learned a stable partition, while reconstruction and perceptual metrics test the recovered waveform.","The paper reports that mirror-stage training outperforms APCodec+ and the non-mirror alternatives on its objective measures, with lower reconstruction error and fewer training epochs/cost.","The speech data, bitrate/downsampling setting, discriminators, metrics, and baselines bound the result; reconstruction quality does not by itself prove usefulness for every TTS or speech-language-model task."),
"franzreb25_interspeech":("Speech anonymization should hide who spoke while keeping the words and useful voice behavior, but a recognition attacker may exploit details that the designer did not intend to preserve.","Changing the target voice can damage intelligibility, and a single equal-error-rate score cannot say whether the attacker used phones, pitch, duration, or another cue.","Convert speech to a random target voice and judge privacy only with one speaker-recognition score.","Make the conversion interpretable: predict phones and durations, cluster target features by phone, and vary phonetic variation and duration separately to locate the identity leakage.","Private kNN-VC replaces source WavLM features with target neighbors, then controls phone variation through per-phone k-means clusters and duration through a predictor; it is evaluated under VoicePrivacy 2024 with utility and privacy measures.","The system treats identity as information distributed across several speech dimensions; changing one dimension at a time turns the attacker score into a probe of what survives anonymization, while phone prediction uses cross-entropy and CTC.","The paper reports that controlling phonetic variation and prosodic factors improves privacy, but target-speaker selection materially changes EER and can make the attack appear weaker without changing utility.","The attacker, target-selection algorithm, English phone inventory, single-speaker duration training, and VoicePrivacy protocol bound the inference; privacy against this recognizer is not universal anonymity or protection against text/style inference."),
"dewhurst25_interspeech":("Researchers and clinicians need to measure how much sound escapes through the nose, but commercial nasometers are expensive and hard to customize, limiting data collection across communities.","Nasalance is a ratio of nasal to total acoustic energy, so microphone placement, cross-signal bleed, baffle shape, and speaker anatomy can change the number even when the speech is comparable.","Infer nasality from a spectrum alone or treat a cheap two-microphone device as interchangeable with a commercial instrument without calibration.","Build open hardware whose microphone, baffle, and analog path can be changed, then compare raw scores and phonological contrasts against a commercial device.","Nosey is a 3-D-printable baffle with replaceable dual microphone clips and open files; the study compares it with an icSpeech device for speakers and phonological environments.","Nasalance is computed as nasal energy divided by nasal plus oral energy; the important test is whether oral/nasal contrasts and their variation are preserved, not whether raw percentages match exactly.","Nosey produces consistently higher raw nasalance scores, but preserves comparable phonological-environment contrasts under the tested conditions and offers a lower-cost customizable platform.","The tested speakers, microphones, baffle geometry, placement, and phonological materials bound the comparison; raw-score offsets and cross-signal bleed prevent treating Nosey and commercial values as directly interchangeable."),
"dao25_interspeech":("A voice assistant needs spoken command examples in a low-resource language, but there may be no good text-to-speech system with which to synthesize them.","Text instructions and spoken instructions share meaning but not the same signal, so training only on text risks losing the acoustic path needed at inference time.","Translate text instructions into speech with a weak TTS system, or fine-tune only on written commands and hope the speech encoder bridges the gap.","Generate synthetic instruction examples only up to a semantic representation, align those representations with a pretrained speech encoder, and train the language model without waveform synthesis.","Speechless uses text-generated instructions, aligns their semantic representations with Whisper encoder representations, and fine-tunes an LLM so it can process spoken commands in low-resource settings.","The method removes the unavailable waveform generator from the training loop while retaining a shared semantic space; alignment is the bridge between written supervision and spoken input.","The paper reports that speech-instruction training without TTS can preserve spoken-instruction understanding and offers a simpler route for low-resource languages.","The language, synthetic text, Whisper encoder, alignment quality, and downstream command tasks bound the result; semantic alignment is not proof that pronunciation, prosody, or real user speech are fully represented."),
"jin25d_interspeech":("A user may want the same words spoken by a different person in a different environment, such as a voice heard through a hallway or in a car, while keeping the source message unchanged.","Speaker timbre and environmental acoustics both change the waveform and can interfere with one another, especially when paired examples for every combination do not exist.","Train one entangled converter and describe the target only with a speaker recording, or apply room filtering after voice conversion as an independent afterthought.","Represent target speaker and environment as separate text-controlled attributes, then retrieve timbre evidence and generate the combined result with a latent diffusion converter.","TES-VC uses synthetic data with decoupled vocal/environment features, a retrieval-based timbre-control module, and text descriptions for both target timbre and acoustic environment.","The desired output is a composition of content, speaker, and room factors; independent controls are tested by changing one description while holding the others fixed and measuring content retention and controllability.","The paper reports effective text-driven control of timbre and environment with high content retention and results on in-domain and out-of-domain conditions.","Synthetic training mixtures, text descriptions, diffusion sampling, evaluation speakers and rooms, and the notion of controllability bound the result; independent factors are operational test dimensions, not guaranteed physical causes."),
"hartanto25_interspeech":("A separator hears speech after room reflections, noise, microphone placement, and speaker positions have mixed together; estimating those conditions can help it decide what belongs to whom.","Treating all variation as nuisance forces the separator to explain location and reverberation inside a speech representation, where they can be confused with phonetic content.","Train only a separation loss and ask the network to become invariant to every room and microphone change.","Predict separation together with speaker and microphone locations and room acoustic parameters, using those physical estimates to disambiguate the speech representation.","SepVAC jointly separates speech and estimates speaker location, microphone-array location, and room parameters on SMS-WSJ-Plus, with curriculum learning used to stabilize the multi-task training.","Auxiliary physical targets constrain the hidden representation: the model is rewarded when it both recovers speech and explains the path that altered it; WER measures the downstream recognition consequence.","The paper reports a 0.67-point WER improvement over SpatialNet on its evaluation and argues that explicit condition estimation improves robustness across acoustic conditions.","SMS-WSJ-Plus, task weights, curriculum schedule, room parameters, and WER bound the claim; joint estimation does not prove that each learned feature corresponds to a unique physical variable."),
"choi25g_interspeech":("Speech recognition may correctly hear a sentence but write it in a form different from what a downstream application expects: numbers, punctuation, abbreviations, and spoken forms can all encode the same meaning.","Most speech databases provide only one transcription convention, so a recognizer cannot learn when to preserve spoken wording and when to normalize into written wording without expensive paired labels.","Normalize every transcript with hand-written rules, or train a recognizer on whichever form appears most often and treat the other form as an error.","Create paired spoken/written text with an LLM, expand it through iterative supervised and semi-supervised learning, and use one bidirectional model for both text-normalization directions.","The BTC model maps spoken to written form and written to spoken form; generated dual transcripts supply training pairs and the model is evaluated on text-conversion quality alongside recognition behavior.","The central object is not a new sound representation but a boundary convention: the same recognized content is rewritten under a task-specific output contract, so conversion errors are distinct from acoustic errors.","The paper reports improved bidirectional text conversion and shows that automatically generated dual transcription data can reduce the cost of constructing paired resources.","LLM-generated text quality, language conventions, iterative filtering, and conversion metrics bound the claim; written-form accuracy does not establish that the underlying ASR heard the speech correctly."),
"chou25_interspeech":("A voice-conversion system should change emotional expression for a speaker it has never seen while preserving the words and recognizable identity.","Emotion is expressed through many coupled changes in pitch, timing, energy, and voice quality, so pushing one style label can distort content or speaker traits; unseen speakers add another source of variation.","Train a separate converter for each target speaker or force an unseen speaker into the closest training identity.","Use a diffusion converter with disentangled content, speaker, and emotion paths plus expressive guidance so emotion can be changed without overwriting the other factors.","ZSDEVC trains on a large emotional-speech corpus and evaluates zero-shot conversion on unseen speakers in both in-domain and out-of-domain datasets, using diffusion generation and separate conditioning signals.","Diffusion supplies a gradual reconstruction path while disentangled conditions define which information should remain fixed; emotion accuracy, naturalness, similarity, and content measures test the competing goals.","The paper reports expressive converted speech with high emotional accuracy, naturalness, and content/speaker preservation on its zero-shot evaluations.","Training corpus, emotion labels, unseen-speaker split, out-of-domain data, and subjective metrics bound the claim; a successful conversion score does not prove that emotion and identity are physically independent."),
"gu25_interspeech":("A singer or speaker may need the same recorded phrase moved to a new pitch while retaining its timing, timbre, and natural vocal quality.","Pitch, vocal-tract resonances, and source characteristics are entangled in the waveform, and paired examples at every original and target pitch are scarce.","Shift the waveform with a fixed signal-processing rule or train a supervised mapper that requires matched in-tune and out-of-tune examples.","Learn a pitch representation and use cycle consistency so a converter can move pitch and return it without losing the source information, even without paired training examples.","Neurodyne uses representation learning and a cycle-consistency GAN to manipulate pitch; pitch and non-pitch features are separated through learned representations and evaluated on singing-voice conversion behavior.","Cycle consistency supplies a testable conservation rule: converting to a target pitch and back should recover the original, while the pitch representation controls the intended change.","The paper reports improved pitch manipulation and synthesis quality over classical and neural comparisons under its singing-voice experiments.","Training voices, pitch range, unpaired-data assumptions, cycle losses, and musical evaluation bound the claim; a successful pitch change does not establish general speaker/style disentanglement."),
"hao25_interspeech":("A hearing aid must amplify speech without feeding the receiver's sound back into its microphone, and it must do so with little delay and little computation.","The acoustic coupling changes over time, while suppressing feedback can also suppress speech; full-band neural processing may be too slow or expensive for a wearable device.","Use a fixed notch filter or a large neural model that estimates the entire waveform with no explicit latency or complexity constraint.","Estimate the desired speech's complex spectrum in time-frequency bands and adapt the feedback canceller with closed-loop fine tuning while keeping the model small.","L3C-DeepMFC uses complex spectrum mapping, full- and sub-band recurrent components, and closed-loop fine tuning for marginal feedback cancellation; evaluation varies feedback paths and reports latency, complexity, and speech quality.","The complex spectrum keeps magnitude and phase, while a closed loop uses the residual error created by the receiver-microphone path to update cancellation; the system is judged on both suppression and preserved speech.","The paper reports low-latency, low-complexity feedback cancellation with improved speech quality relative to its baselines under tested hearing-aid conditions.","Feedback paths, delay budget, hardware assumptions, noise, and quality metrics bound the result; lab cancellation performance is not the same as clinical benefit for every listener."),
}
